    {
      id: "dalarna",
      ime: "Dalarna",
      vrsta: "regija",
      sazetak: "The province that Swedes consider the heart of the country: red cottages around Lake Siljan, little wooden horses, an old copper mine and the loveliest Midsummer celebrations.",
      prica: [
        "Dalarna, which means the valleys, is a province of forests and lakes in central Sweden. It was from here that Gustav Vasa tried in 1520 to rouse the farmers to rise up against the Danes, and when they changed their minds, two skiers caught up with him on his way to Norway. In memory of that, the Vasaloppet ski marathon, 90 kilometers long, has been held every March since 1922.",
        "For centuries the wealth came from the copper mine in Falun, and a by-product of the mining is the red paint that colors wooden houses all over Sweden. In the late 19th century the painters Carl Larsson and Anders Zorn moved here, and their pictures of village life shaped the Swedes' idea of what a home looks like."
      ],
      vidjeti: [
        { ime: "The copper mine in Falun (Falu Gruva)", opis: "Copper was mined here for at least a thousand years, right up to 1992, and in the 17th century the mine supplied about two thirds of Europe's copper and paid for Sweden's wars. The huge pit Stora Stöten was created by a collapse on Midsummer's Eve in 1687, when, fortunately, nobody was in the mine. With a guide you go 67 meters underground, and you will also hear the story of the miner Mats, whose body was found perfectly preserved in 1719, 42 years after the accident, and was recognized by his former fiancée. The mine is on the UNESCO list." },
        { ime: "Carl Larsson's home in Sundborn", opis: "The painter Carl Larsson and his wife Karin, an artist herself, decorated the house Lilla Hyttnäs with bright colors, simple furniture and textiles they made themselves, the complete opposite of the dark and cluttered salons of the time. His watercolors of family life made the house famous, and it is considered the source of the Swedish style of home living. It still belongs to the family and is visited on a guided tour." },
        { ime: "The Zorn Museum and house in Mora", opis: "Anders Zorn, born in Mora in 1860, was one of the most sought-after portraitists of his day and also painted three presidents of the USA. He returned to his home region and painted bathers on the lake and village dances. Beside the museum is his house with a great hall in the Viking style, preserved just as his wife Emma left it." },
        { ime: "The wooden horse workshops in Nusnäs", opis: "In two family workshops, founded in the 1920s, you can watch the whole process for free: from sawing the pine and carving with a knife to dipping in paint and painting the pattern called kurbits, which is done with two colors on the same brush." },
        { ime: "Lake Siljan, Rättvik and Leksand", opis: "The lake fills part of a crater made by a meteorite about 377 million years ago, the largest in Europe. In Rättvik a wooden pier 628 meters long runs out into the lake, built in 1895 so that steamboats could dock in the shallow water. In summer the long church boats glide by here, the ones in which farmers used to row to Sunday service." },
        { ime: "Dalhalla", opis: "An abandoned limestone quarry near Rättvik, sixty meters deep, with an emerald lake at the bottom, has since the 1990s been a summer stage with outstanding acoustics, where operas and concerts are held." }
      ],
      jesti: [
        { ime: "Falukorv", opis: "A thick, mild sausage in a red casing that originated in Falun, where ropes for the mine were braided from ox hide and the meat had to be used somehow. Today it is an everyday dish for Swedish families, baked in the oven with mustard and cheese." },
        { ime: "Knäckebröd from Leksand", opis: "The best-known Swedish crispbread is baked in Leksand in large round discs, and in the factory shop it is sold still warm." },
        { ime: "Blueberry soup (blåbärssoppa)", opis: "A thick, sweet bilberry soup that is handed out warm to skiers at the Vasaloppet and drunk cold in summer." }
      ],
      dozivjeti: [
        { ime: "Going down into the Falun mine", opis: "The tour lasts about an hour, and down below it is five degrees and wet, so take a jacket and sturdy shoes. Helmets and capes are handed out at the entrance.", link: "https://www.falugruva.se/en/" },
        { ime: "Painting your own little horse", opis: "In Nusnäs you can buy an unpainted horse and a brush, or simply watch the craftswomen at their workbenches.", link: "https://nilsolsson.se/en/home/" },
        { ime: "Midsummer in Leksand", opis: "The largest celebration in the country draws thousands of people in folk costume. The pole arrives by church boat and is raised by hand to the music of fiddles, and then people dance until midnight, which is bright here in June." },
        { ime: "Carl Larsson's house", opis: "Tours are in small groups and fill up quickly in summer, so reserve your ticket in advance.", link: "https://carllarsson.se/en/" }
      ],
      agencije: [
        { ime: "Visit Dalarna", opis: "The province's official tourist board.", link: "https://www.visitdalarna.se/en" },
        { ime: "Zornmuseet", opis: "The museum organizes guided tours of the painter's house and studio.", link: "https://zorn.se/en/" }
      ],
      kada: "From June to August, and if you can choose, come for Midsummer, on the Friday between June 19 and 25. The train from Stockholm to Falun or Leksand takes about two and a half to three hours."
    }
